     <div class=\"s-lg-icons pad-left-sm\"><ul class=\"\"><li><a href=\"http://www.library.ucla.edu/service/campus-access\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"Requires UCLA authentication\" class=\"s-lg-icon\" src=\"//d2jv02qf7xgjwx.cloudfront.net/sites/705/icons/983/key-newblue-transp.gif\"/><i class=\"fa fa-fw fa-external-link \" \n    aria-hidden=\"true\"\n           title=\"This link opens in a new window\"\n   ></i><span class=\"sr-only\">This link opens in a new window</span></a> </li></ul></div>\n                                                                            </div>\n            <div class=\"s-lg-gtitle\" >\n                                <a  target=&quot;_blank&quot;  href=\"https://referenceworks.brillonline.com/browse/brill-s-encyclopedia-of-the-religions-of-the-indigenous-people-of-south-asia-online\" onclick=\"return springSpace.springTrack.trackLink({link: this,_st_type_id: '16',_st_content_id: '51433284',_st_inc_return: this});\">\n                                                                Brill&#039;s Encyclopedia of the Religions of the Indigenous People of South Asia Online\n                                                        </a>\n                                \n            </div>\n            <div class=\"s-lg-az-result-description\">Reflects the diversity of indigenous cultures of South Asia with its many language groups and religious traditions. Religion is taken in a broad sense and includes aspects of morality, symbolism, identity formation, environmental concerns, and art.</div>\n                    </div>\n    </div>\n</div>\n<div>\n    <div class=\"s-lib-box s-lib-border-round s-lib-box-idx-guide-list\">\n        <div class=\"s-lib-box-content\">\n            <div class=\"s-lg-az-result-badges s-lg-gmeta pull-right s-lg-small s-lib-color-lt-grey\">\n                <div class=\"s-lg-icons pad-left-sm\"><ul class=\"\"><li><a href=\"http://www.library.ucla.edu/service/campus-access\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"Requires UCLA authentication\" class=\"s-lg-icon\" src=\"//d2jv02qf7xgjwx.cloudfront.net/sites/705/icons/983/key-newblue-transp.gif\"/><i class=\"fa fa-fw fa-external-link \" \n    aria-hidden=\"true\"\n           title=\"This link opens in a new window\"\n   ></i><span class=\"sr-only\">This link opens in a new window</span></a> </li></ul></div>\n                                                                            </div>\n            <div class=\"s-lg-gtitle\" >\n                                <a  target=&quot;_blank&quot;  href=\"http://www.researchsource.amdigital.co.uk/MissStudies\" onclick=\"return springSpace.springTrack.trackLink({link: this,_st_type_id: '16',_st_content_id: '51135871',_st_inc_return: this});\">\n                                                                Missionary Studies\n                                                        </a>\n                                \n            </div>\n            <div class=\"s-lg-az-result-description\">These sources are resources for the study of missionary work, educational work, medical work, evangelism, political conflict, and the emergence of indigenous churches. The collections are global, with Africa, East and South Asia, Australasia and the Pacific, and the Americas all represented. The sources will be of interest to scholars in a range of fields, from missiology to colonial history and anthropology. Highlights include:  Papers of Reverend George Brown (1835-1917), Methodist missionary and ethnographer; records of female missionaries and women's missionary organizations.</div>\n                    </div>\n    </div>\n</div>\n</div></div>","experts":"<div class=\"margin-bottom-xlg\"><div class=\"s-lib-public-side-header\"><h2 class=\"pad-bottom-sm\">Philosophy & Religion Experts</h2></div><div class=\"txt pad-top-sm\"><div class=\"s-lib-featured-profile-spacer clearfix\"></div><div class=\"s-lib-featured-profile-container\"><a href=\"https://guides.library.ucla.ed